#: package/contents/ui/config/configAutomation.qml:149
msgid ""
"Listens with the microphone every few minutes while music is playing and "
"quietly re-tunes the sync when the speakers have drifted apart. The check "
"rides on a tone too high to hear — the music keeps playing and most people "
"hear nothing. It runs only while a Bluetooth speaker is in the group, never "
"during a recording or an alarm, and audio never leaves this computer."
msgstr ""

#: package/contents/ui/config/configAutomation.qml:157
msgid "Live radio"
msgstr ""

#: package/contents/ui/config/configAutomation.qml:163
msgid "When a stream dies:"
msgstr ""

#: package/contents/ui/config/configAutomation.qml:164
msgid "Try to get it back"
msgstr ""

#: package/contents/ui/config/configAutomation.qml:167
msgid ""
"A station that goes quiet is tried again at widening intervals: half a "
"minute, then a minute, then two. A stream that really dropped is back well "
"inside that. If it is still silent afterwards the widget lets it go and "
"stays quiet — it will not put the station on again by itself when your "
"connection returns later, and that part is the whole point. Turn this off "
"and a dead stream stops at once, the way most players behave. An alarm is "
"bound by none of it: a wake-up keeps trying."
msgstr ""

